## Typed FFI returns — Atomic surface.
##
## Source: docs/specs/types/typed_ffi_returns.spec.md (B8 row for Atomic*).
##
## AtomicI64 is non-generic, so per spec B10 its `.new -> Int` does NOT
## auto-lift. The lib-decl in `library/std/sync/src/lib.rvn` declares
## `def self.new ... -> AtomicI64` EXPLICITLY (the structured return is
## the source of truth — spec B2). Without that explicit declaration,
## `AtomicI64.new(0).fetch_add(5)` would error at typeck because the
## `.fetch_add` resolution would lookup methods on `Int`.

def main
  let a = AtomicI64.new(0)
  let prev = a.fetch_add(5)
  let cur = a.load
  if prev == 0 && cur == 5
    puts "ok"
  else
    puts "fail"
  end
end
